Hello VoxelMatters team,

you covered Solidon3D in detail on 22 August, so this is not a second product
introduction — only what has genuinely been added since the state you
described.

At the time, the result of an edit was a triangle mesh. As of 0.5.0 it is an
exact body: primitives are built with real faces and edges, and holes, slots,
countersinks, bosses, beads, grooves and threads stay exact when they are
moved, duplicated, rotated or removed. STEP goes in and comes back out
cleanly.

The part that changes the story rather than extending the feature list is that
the choice disappeared. Two geometry kernels run under one interface, and the
four options that used to switch between them have been removed. The user does
not decide between two modes; Solidon keeps the exact body as long as it can
and says so when it cannot. Existing projects keep computing unchanged.

The second addition is the one that photographs well: a honeycomb pattern, a
knurl, ribs, waves or knobs used to fill the object tree with hundreds of
faces. They are now one feature with pitch, cell width and depth — removed
with a click, reapplied with three numbers, including around a handle. A
texture on a cylinder follows the curvature, so grooves are equally deep
everywhere and the pattern closes around the circumference without a seam.

Shorter items:

* Dimensions are edited on the model itself, with a live preview, instead of
  in a dialog placed in front of it.
* An existing thread gets its counterpart on the other part at the press of a
  button, in a table size and as a fit.
* Resin printers are supported, with pixel size and minimum wall.
* A model with open areas is closed while it is read instead of merely
  reported.
* Recognition is several times faster; moving a 200,000-triangle model answers
  in half a second instead of eight.

70 user-visible changes in this release; 896 since the first 0.1 demo.

Solidon3D is a desktop application for Windows, macOS and Linux. One-time
purchase, no subscription, no account: after a single activation it runs fully
offline. Interface and manual are available in six languages, and there is a
demo.

I am happy to provide a review licence, print-resolution images or answers to
any question directly.

